{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01TC4kSem9RXZbMNCfhJkdjA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-folder, stdlib-only personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that has grown into a trio-driven R&D mission-control. Grounded from the project docs:\n\n- **Purpose â€” a personal productivity system.** It manages tasks, projects, and captured ideas across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) using **plain markdown files as the single source of truth** (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) â€” no database, no lock files. Tasks move through a lifecycle: active â†’ done / cancelled / saved-for-later / restored.\n\n- **What it ships â€” a local web app + CLI over those files.** `anchor_gui.py` is the primary interface: a self-contained Python HTTP server that regenerates the full dashboard HTML on each request, writes changes back to markdown, and runs **persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`** (host `PUTER`/`gwl-server`). `anchor.py` mirrors the same logic as a CLI and also emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It's stdlib-only with one declared exception.** No external dependencies except the optional `pywinpty` (`import winpty`, lazy, in `pty_manager.py` only, `pip install .[terminal]`) for the real terminal subsystem; `distro.py`'s import scan enforces this rule and refuses any other native/third-party import in product code.\n\n- **It self-tests daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler â€” it parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server on a test port, exercises every endpoint and the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (fully stubbed, never live `claude`), walks a synthetic task through every state, and writes `health_reports/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n\n- **Its main evolution is the \"R&D Control Surface,\" now at v4 \"Project Cockpit\" (built + merged to master 2026-06-13).** This turns each project into a single-screen cockpit for the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** trio: lane tiles with one honest status light (green/amber/red/grey), inline expanding panels combining a cached summary on top with a real resizable **xterm.js terminal over ConPTY** below, per-session **git-worktree isolation**, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini, Gemini research-only), per-lane doc-roles, a cost/tokens/time rollup, a grass-idea board, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **It's branded as a Ghost World Labs tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\"** using the vendored `vendor/brand/gwl-m-icon.svg` mark (also the favicon).\n\nThese claims come from `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North-Star/decision anchors in the v3/v4 planning docs. I did not re-read source files to verify each one â€” say the word if you want me to ground any specific claim against the actual code rather than the docs."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3daaa5c-a931-42f5-b050-70f4c2aaad72","uuid":"98099d73-312e-403f-b4cd-3528d245d846","request_id":"req_011Cc1fCUe6asU6nM5ofnz8z"}
